Boussinesq flow, natural convection, plumes and instability (@fd-buoyant: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @fluid-dynamics, #source "../sources/Fluid-Mechanics-Tong.lingua#r_3SP698XHQFSZZ6N9Q22NESHMEA", #source "../sources/Advanced-Fluid-Dynamics-Mei-MIT.lingua#r_21NXVH78F0NYDPDVTG66PG261P", #source "../sources/Mecanica-dos-Fluidos-e-Transportes-Gobbi-Dias.lingua#r_1F9KHVCP86X68RR7DTZASE5F1J", #fluid-dynamics "Rotating-flow-Rossby-number-and-geostrophic-balance.lingua#r_6X74505055WATA2XZ7CD18HQYZ", #clean-manufacturing "../../../production/clean-manufacturing-and-contamination-control/facilities/Buoyancy-and-wind-can-compete-with-mechanical-pressure.lingua#r_44PV55ESMT6BHNTS2DT5XSA4JS") { r_3D346A9GVA8D8T39K4KHG0X3W0
**Read:** [Fluid Mechanics — David Tong](../sources/Fluid-Mechanics-Tong.lingua#r_3SP698XHQFSZZ6N9Q22NESHMEA), chapter 5 Rayleigh–Bénard convection and Boussinesq approximation; [Advanced fluid dynamics — Mei notes and MIT modules](../sources/Advanced-Fluid-Dynamics-Mei-MIT.lingua#r_21NXVH78F0NYDPDVTG66PG261P), chapter 4 buoyant plume and thermal approximations; [Introdução à Mecânica dos Fluidos e aos Fenômenos de Transporte — Gobbi and colleagues](../sources/Mecanica-dos-Fluidos-e-Transportes-Gobbi-Dias.lingua#r_1F9KHVCP86X68RR7DTZASE5F1J), coupled differential energy and momentum equations.

The Boussinesq approximation retains small density departures in buoyancy while treating density as constant in selected inertial and continuity terms. Derive the approximation from a small relative density change and declared scales. A low Mach number by itself does not justify it, and a large temperature or composition range can defeat it.

Couple the momentum equation with heat or solute transport. Identify the Rayleigh, Prandtl or Schmidt numbers and the geometry-specific conditions determining the base state and instability. A critical Rayleigh number belongs to particular boundaries and mode assumptions; it is not a universal convection threshold for every enclosure.

Compare a heated horizontal layer, an isolated buoyant plume and a stably stratified withdrawal. Track heat or buoyancy flux as well as velocity. Connect the general fluid mechanism to [Flow fields, advection and the fluid energy equation](../../thermodynamics-and-heat-transfer/convection/Flow-fields-advection-and-the-fluid-energy-equation.lingua#r_2WC51KRYYZ7BRAT3ASQRMTKTDT), keeping wall thermal conditions and property variation explicit. A visible circulation pattern is only one part of the energy and mixing account.

**Continue:** [Rotating flow, Rossby number and geostrophic balance](Rotating-flow-Rossby-number-and-geostrophic-balance.lingua#r_6X74505055WATA2XZ7CD18HQYZ).

